From e982e55094a52d6ddc409fa72cd883e469f3bae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: Add a stateless H.265 encoder

Add v4l2slh265enc for encoders that implement the HEVC stateless encode
uAPI (V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_ENCODE_PARAMS), such as the RK3588 VEPU580.

The kernel writes the VPS, SPS, PPS and slice segment headers and keeps
the reconstructed pictures, which are identified by the timestamp of the
OUTPUT buffer they were encoded from. The element sets the SPS and PPS
once (8x8 to 64x64 coding blocks, 4x4 to 32x32 transforms, SAO and TMVP
as properties) and gives each picture its NAL unit type, picture order
count and reference picture set: IDR_W_RADL pictures, then TRAIL_R P
pictures that reference the previous picture. The average QP of each
picture is read from V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_ENCODE_FEEDBACK for the vbr
rate control.

The output is Main profile; the kernel picks the lowest level that fits.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265enc.c | 404 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265enc.h |  34 +++
 sys/v4l2codecs/meson.build           |   2 +
 sys/v4l2codecs/plugin.c              |   7 +
 4 files changed, 447 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265enc.c
 create mode 100644 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codech265enc.h

